{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Eliashib the high priest be[Eb]gan
[Cm]Rebuilding the Sheep Gate a[D]gain
[Gm]They consecrated it [Eb]with care
[Cm]Set doors and bolted them [D]there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Gm]Next to them Meremoth [Eb]worked on
Repairs for the c[Cm]ity strong
Meshullam son of Berec[D]hiah
Made repairs as the wall [Gm]grew
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Zadok son of Baana [Eb]joined
Next to them their labor [Cm]joined
Men of Tekoa made re[D]pairs
But nobles would not lift their [Gm]cares
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
On the twen-[Eb]ty-fifth of E[Cm]lul
The wall was finished, it [D]was full
In fif-ty-two days it [Gm]stood
Against all the [Eb]enemy’s mood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Cm]They knew it was our [D]God
{end_of_verse}

